 "notes": [
  "Dynamic-edge line convention: for a split statement (EXEC CICS on one line, XCTL PROGRAM(...) on the next) I used the first physical line of the statement (the EXEC CICS line) both as evidence and in the ?dynamic id, e.g. COMEN01C:184/201, CORPT00C:548, COTRN00C:192/518, COUSR00C:196/206/514. The XCTL keyword itself is one line later. Only COMEN01C:156 has EXEC CICS XCTL on one line.",
  "COMEN01C:148 EXEC CICS INQUIRE PROGRAM(CDEMO-MENU-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION)) is not a CALL/LINK/XCTL, so no edge. COMEN01C XCTL at 156 and 184 use the subscripted name CDEMO-MENU-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION), dynamic only per rule 4 (no candidates), even though COMEN02Y VALUE literals list COACTVWC, COACTUPC, COCRDLIC, COCRDSLC, COCRDUPC, COTRN00C, COTRN01C, COTRN02C, CORPT00C, COBIL00C, COPAUS0C (COMEN02Y.cpy lines 28-89).",
  "CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (COCOM01Y, PIC X(08), no VALUE) is the target of the XCTL in 9 of 10 programs. Every literal moved to it anywhere in the program yields a candidate at every XCTL site in that program. MOVE CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (COTRN01C:119, COTRN02C:140, COUSR02C:116, COUSR03C:115) is a non-literal move, so it only reinforces the dynamic remainder. MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM at COMEN01C:83 is FROM not TO, ignored.",
  "COSGN00C XCTL PROGRAM('COADM01C') at 231 and 'COMEN01C' at 236 are plain literals (multi-line EXEC CICS XCTL, the EXEC CICS XCTL keywords are on the evidence line).",
  "CORPT00C:517 EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') is a transient data queue write, not a CICS FILE operation, so no data edge. The program builds inline JCL text (lines 81-127, '//STEP10 EXEC PROC=TRANREPT') as string literals, no edge from it.",
  "CICS file names come from WORKING-STORAGE VALUE items with trailing blanks ('USRSEC  ', 'TRANSACT', 'CCXREF  ', 'CXACAIX '); none is ever the receiving field of MOVE/STRING/READ INTO in these programs, so all are rule 1 constants. CSD DEFINE FILE entries: CCXREF app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:37-40, CXACAIX 63-66, TRANSACT 76-78, USRSEC 88-90.",
  "COTRN02C:40 WS-ACCTDAT-FILE VALUE 'ACCTDAT ' is declared but never used in an EXEC CICS statement, so no ACCTDAT edge. COTRN02C also copies CVACT01Y (ACCOUNT-RECORD) with no file operation using it, so it is an include only.",
  "COTRN01C READ ... UPDATE (269) has no REWRITE anywhere in the program, so mode is read. COUSR03C DELETE (307) has no FROM/INTO, layout_copybooks taken from its READ INTO(SEC-USER-DATA) at 269 (CSUSR01Y defines 01 SEC-USER-DATA).",
  "DFHAID and DFHBMSCA are not in app/cpy or app/cpy-bms, so ext:. COMEN01, CORPT00, COSGN00, COTRN00-02, COUSR00-03 are BMS symbolic-map copybooks in app/cpy-bms (stems match ignoring case), so cpy:. COSGN00C:59 '*COPY DFHATTR.' is a comment (column 7 asterisk), no edge.",
